WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
Thanks for joining me on fascinating frontiers, episode 136.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.820
Today is July 19, 2026, some fascinating developments to cover today.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.940
NASA's psyche spacecraft just used Mars as a gravitational sling shot,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.240
returning a rich data set that will sharpen its approach to a metal world never visited before.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.120
The spacecraft completed its planned gravity assist maneuver at Mars

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.940
and transmitted a full data set from the encounter.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.700
Mission teams are now analyzing images and spectra collected during the closest approach

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.360
to refine navigation for the 2029 arrival at asteroid psyche.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.820
The flyby also served as an in-flight test of several instruments ahead of the main science phase.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.200
No hardware anomalies were reported during the past.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.200
The next major milestone is a second deep space maneuver later this year.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:59.140
Early spectra from the encounter may already offer hints about the asteroid's surface composition.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.420
The data will also help test autonomous systems in deep space conditions.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:11.360
On a different note, the finished built ICI-EX-73 synthetic aperture radar satellite

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.660
has been formally registered under UN document

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:23.400
ser.eslash1346 as key A01 and is now owned by the Portuguese Air Force.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:31.200
ICI has previously sold identical radar satellites to operators in the United States, Poland, Greece,

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.560
the United Arab Emirates, and Brazil.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.080
The move marks the first Portuguese military ownership of an orbital radar asset.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.380
Portugal joins a growing list of nations acquiring commercial radar constellations

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.080
for sovereign surveillance needs.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:52.100
If Earth were a basketball, the altitude of most radar satellites would be roughly the thickness of

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.700
a sheet of paper above its surface. Yet from that narrow corridor, they map every continent

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:03.780
regardless of weather. A synthetic aperture radar satellite sends out its own microwave pulses

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:09.860
and records the faint echoes that bounce back. The signal never waits for sunlight or clear skies

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:16.460
the way optical cameras must. One satellite traveling at roughly 7.5 kilometers per second

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:21.780
can synthesize an antenna hundreds of meters wide, simply by moving along its orbit.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.100
The same pass can distinguish between open water, forest canopy, and urban structures

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:33.560
because each surface scatters microwaves differently. Scientists still cannot predict exactly how

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:39.200
vegetation moisture or soil salinity will alter the return signal strength from one season to

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:46.000
the next. Astronomers have captured the dimest directly imaged exoplanet to date using ground-based

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.520
instruments. The detection pushes current adaptive optics and coronagraph technology to new limits

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:59.020
for separating planet light from host star glare. No mass or orbital period figures were released

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:05.020
in the initial announcement. Future observations will attempt to extract atmospheric spectra from

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:11.400
the same target. The sub-millimeter array on Mauna Kea has demonstrated its new semi-automated

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.960
alert system by rapidly sluing to a gamma ray burst detected by space-based telescopes.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.240
The interferometer recorded sub-millimeter emission within minutes of the trigger.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.120
Data from the event will help constrain the physics of relativistic jets launched by the burst

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:34.420
progenitor. The successful test shows how ground-based radio arrays can now respond on time scales

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:40.540
previously limited to optical facilities. Researchers suggest that massive planets could register

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.780
interactions with dark matter particles through measurable orbital or atmospheric effects.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:52.120
The idea leverages the large cross-section of gas and ice giants to capture rare events that

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:58.320
smaller worlds would miss. No observational campaign has yet been funded to test the hypothesis.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.800
If validated, the method would offer a novel complement to underground detectors and space-based

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:11.740
instruments. Modeling papers outlining expected signatures are in preparation. The proposal draws on

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:17.520
the planet's substantial volume and gravitational influence to increase the probability of detectable

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.200
particle encounters. Further theoretical work is examining whether atmospheric heating or

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.340
slight orbital perturbations could serve as observable markers. The national security space launch

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:37.200
phase 3 lane 1 contract maximum value has been increased from $5.6 billion to $17 billion to

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:43.160
accommodate rising launch demand. The adjustment provides headroom for additional national security

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:49.120
payloads scheduled through the end of the decade. Lane 1 covers medium lift missions that do not

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.740
require the heaviest lift capacity. Industry teams are already positioning for the expanded

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:01.520
opportunity pool. Defense Production Act funding of $7.1 million has been awarded to Martin

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:08.560
Material Solutions to scale manufacturing of radiation resistant cover glass. The material protects solar

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:15.120
arrays and thermal control systems on spacecraft from charged particle damage. The small business will

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.400
add production capacity at its existing facility. First deliveries from the expanded line are expected

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:28.260
within two years. Japan's RVX Experimental Vehicle Lifted Off reached a controlled altitude

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:34.760
and executed a successful vertical landing in its inaugural test flight. The prototype is designed

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:41.240
to demonstrate technologies for future reusable first stages. Telemetry from the flight is now being

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:47.160
reviewed to assess engine performance and guidance accuracy. Additional flights are planned to

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:53.340
expand the performance envelope. Remember, the show covered Artemis developments on the last episode.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:06:01.220
NASA will fly an uncrewed Artemis 3 demonstration mission in 2027 to practice rendezvous and docking

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:07.320
between a commercial human landing system and the Orion spacecraft. Data gathered during the rehearsal

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:14.560
will validate procedures ahead of the crude landing targeted for 2028. The mission also serves as an

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:20.980
end-to-end check of ground and flight control teams. The island nation of Mauritius exceeded to the

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:28.080
Artemis Accords on July 17, bringing the total number of signatories to 70 in under six years.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:34.900
Serbia has also signed the Artemis Accords, committing to the same principles of lunar exploration

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:42.080
and data sharing already adopted by 69 other nations. Both nations cited opportunities for future

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:49.760
scientific and industrial collaboration. July 18 marks the birth of John Glenn, who flew 59 combat

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:56.860
missions in World War II and 63 in Korea before becoming one of NASA's original Mercury astronauts.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:04.680
In 1962, he completed three orbits aboard Friendship 7, becoming the first American to circle the

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:12.900
Earth. Glenn later served as a US Senator and returned to space on the 1998 STS-95 Shuttle mission.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:19.200
His career bridged military aviation, early human space flight, and later political service.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:24.460
Archival footage and mission transcripts are being highlighted by NASA this week.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:30.300
The anniversary underscores his role in establishing sustained American presence in orbit.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:36.360
Public events this week include screenings of restored Mercury footage at several planetariums.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:42.900
The Tegasa meteorite dated to 4.1 billion years ago shows evidence of a granite-like crust

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:47.520
and indicates Mars had already begun losing surface water by that epoch.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:53.580
Isotopic measurements suggest the planet's early hydrosphere was diminishing faster than previously

00:07:53.580 --> 00:08:00.120
modeled. The rock provides a rare sample of noakean era crust not yet visited by rovers.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:06.020
Researchers are now comparing its mineralogy with orbital data from current Mars missions.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:13.740
NGC-6563 in Sagittarius is an oval bubble of gas lit by its central white dwarf

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.780
and now stands highest in the evening sky as the moon sets.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:24.180
The nebula formed when the progenitor star shed its outer layers, leaving the hot core to

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:30.940
ionize the expanding shell. Observers with moderate telescopes can locate it near the Sagittarius

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:37.300
teapot asterism. Follow-up imaging this week will capture any changes in the nebula's apparent

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:43.560
brightness as it transits. A new public website displays a complete chronological record of human

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:49.140
space flights from Yuri Gagarin through the most recent Soyuz mission. The single-page

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:54.300
interface allows users to scroll through every crude launch without switching between separate

00:08:54.300 --> 00:09:00.440
databases. The project was built to address the lack of a unified visual history that includes

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:07.560
mission durations and crude details. Keep an eye on further national registrations as ICE continues

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:13.680
expanding its customer base. That covers today's space and science news. Share this with a

